   </dc:creator>
   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Type I and type II errors in hypothesis testing</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">two-dimensional version</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:type>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>Text</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:type>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Two-dimensional diagram of a statistical hypothesis test. A horizontal axis shows values t of the test statistic T</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and a vertical axis shows the density of T. Two bell-shaped normal density curves with the same spread are drawn: the density of T under the null hypothesis H0 in blue on the left</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and the density of T under the alternative hypothesis H1 in dark red on the right. A vertical line at the critical value c</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">marked as a point on the t axis</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">separates the acceptance region to the left</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">shown as a green band below the axis</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">from the critical region to the right</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">shown as an orange band. The curves are labelled Density of T under H0: f sub T of t given theta0</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">and Density of T under H1: f sub T of t given theta1. The bands are labelled Acceptance region (Accept H0) and Critical region (Reject H0). The shaded</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">hatched blue tail of the H0 curve right of c is labelled alpha equals P(Type I error) equals P(Reject H0 given H0 true). The shaded</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">cross-hatched magenta tail of the H1 curve left of c is labelled beta equals P(Type II error) equals P(Accept H0 given H0 false). Two-dimensional companion to a figure adapted from &quot;PPV</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">NPV</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Sensitivity and Specificity&quot; by Luigi Albert Maria</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">Wikimedia Commons</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en">licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:language>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>en</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:language>
   <dc:date>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li>2026-10-29T22:59:54Z</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:date>
